<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The bundle's Info.plist; packaging/macos/bundle.sh fills in @VERSION@.
     The document types put QuickPlay under "Open With" for the formats it
     plays, ranked Alternate so it never takes over as the default player
     unless the user picks it (Get Info, Open with, Change All). Declared by
     extension, as WaveFlow Desktop does: DSF and DFF have no system type,
     and an entry that lists content types has its extensions ignored. The
     files arrive as application:openURLs: (src/macos.rs). .mp4 is left
     out, as in WaveFlow, so QuickPlay is not offered for videos.
     One entry per format, each with its document icon (bundle.sh copies
     packaging/macos/file-icons/*.icns into Resources, file-icons.sh makes
     them), for the files QuickPlay is the default player of: everywhere for
     DSF, DFF, WavPack and APE; for the types macOS declares itself, Finder's icon and list
     views keep the system's icon and Get Info shows this one. -->
